//   precondition gives parser.IsValidPrefix([]). In the complete-prefix branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut to false, so the implication
//   becomes vacuous. In the narrow constrained branch, AdaptiveConstrainedStep
//   returns either eosToken or a token whose append keeps the prefix valid, and
//   AppendConstrainedToken preserves that validity. In the wide constrained
//   branch, the same AdaptiveConstrainedStep postcondition gives validity of
//   currentConstrainedOut + [next], and AppendConstrainedToken preserves it.
// suffix: In the unconstrained branch, if we stay outside then the implication
//   is vacuous; if we enter a span, currentConstrainedOut is [], which matches
//   the length-0 suffix of generated after appending "<<". In the complete-
//   prefix branch, CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most the closing delimiter
